<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Device builds only; see CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in the project, which the simulator
	     overrides with Simulator.entitlements.

	     This file is what the "HealthKit" capability in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab
	     writes. Ticking the box in Xcode and keeping this file produce the same build, so do
	     not do both - Xcode would create a second file and point the target at it.

	     HealthKit needs two separate things and neither one works without the other:
	       - this entitlement, or the first HKHealthStore call fails;
	       - NSHealthShareUsageDescription in Shared/Info.plist, or iOS TERMINATES the app
	         rather than returning an error. That key is in the plist, with the same warning.

	     Automatic signing adds HealthKit to the App ID and reissues the profile, so a fresh
	     clone needs no portal work. A device build without a team still stops earlier, at
	     "requires a development team" - see Signing.xcconfig.

	     We only READ, so there is no com.apple.developer.healthkit.background-delivery here:
	     that one wakes the app on new samples and AAPS has its own loop cadence.

	     The access array is for clinical health records (lab results, medications) from a
	     health provider. AAPS reads none of those, so it stays empty. Xcode writes the empty
	     array too; it requests nothing. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit.access</key>
	<array/>
	<!-- Time Sensitive Notifications. The code already posts urgent alarms with the time-sensitive
	     interruption level (IosSystemNotificationPlatform, IosLoopNotifier); without this
	     entitlement iOS treats them as ordinary notifications, and a Focus mode hides them.
	     Automatic signing adds the capability to the App ID. Critical alerts are a separate
	     entitlement that Apple grants on request only. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
